--
^warning: ignoring
--
A base-object constructor now gives each direct base with virtual bases
tables with that base's overriders and the offsets of the complete object
being constructed, copied from the base's own tables and patched from the
virtual pointers in place, and restores the pointers afterwards (the
Itanium C++ ABI passes a VTT instead).  It also saves and restores the
pointers around a dynamic base without virtual bases (Pad), whose
constructor installs its own tables.  The construction table
virtual_table::V@M@D was missing: do_virtual_table inserted the tables
while iterating over the symbol table.  With the W188 build, assertions 1,
3, 4 and 6 failed.
